From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:20:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 110/191] [ae-patch] Read a dead permission hook's
 approval-wait marker as stale before the TTL

A deploy SIGTERMs the runner while a PreToolUse permission hook is parked,
and the hook dies before its cleanup clears its marker. The next runner then
read the marker as a pending Claude prompt for the whole 420 s TTL and
refused every send with "Answer the pending Claude question or permission
request before sending a message". A live hook refreshes its marker every
60 s, so once a marker is older than APPROVAL_WAIT_ORPHAN_GRACE_S (90 s)
approval_wait_is_fresh probes the pid in its name with process_alive and
treats a gone or zombie process as stale. Younger markers are never probed,
so a hook whose pid reads differently here (a launcher's pid namespace) is
never misjudged, and the probe is Windows-safe. The TTL stays the backstop
for a reused pid or a name with no pid.
